review_text:
I consider myself to be a big fun of Brothers in Arms title, but I can NOT recommend "Hell's Highway".

Yes, that an old game, but I'm not judging based on modern standards. This game is still bad when comparing with its predecessors - "Road to Hill 30" and "Earned in Blood". If you are new to Brothers in Arms title - go and check out "Road to Hill 30" and "Earned in Blood". If you have already seen previous games, then prepare yourself for disappointment.

I've made up some sort of comparison of "Hell's Highway" with previous games:

I'd better start with cons:
 * bad gameplay. There is no more authentic feel like previous game had. This game feels like a game for kids ("Medal of Honor" or smth like that). Health is quickly regenerated. Many covers do not work if you are not 'leaning' (i.e. simply crouching behind cover).
 * bad storytelling. Really. It's awkwardly awful;
 * bad graphics. I don't know why, but graphics from previous games was more appealing;
 * bad audio. Usually I don't really pay attention to this aspect, but audio effect in this game are a bit irritating and unrealistic;

Pros:
 * there are missions where you can drive a tank. This has nothing to do with realism, but still could be nice;
 * environment is a bit more destructible;
 * teams got some special weapons - MG & bazooka.

Brothers In Arms: Hell's Highway
pros:
//fast game with modern day graphics with easy controls that moves from location A to B to C and so on
//good amount of action and special effects
cons:
//some difficult battles
//some lack of directions/instructions

//good game
Personal Suggested Purchase Price: $1.49 Or Less During Sale
